# Debian proper, which needs a per-crate licence audit of all 566 vendored crates.
Files: vendor/*
Copyright: the respective crate authors
License: various
 The vendor directory holds the Rust crate dependencies, vendored so the
 package can be built without network access. Each crate keeps its own licence
 text alongside its source, at vendor/*/LICENSE*, and the crate metadata in
 vendor/*/Cargo.toml records the licence it is distributed under. The great
 majority are MIT or Apache-2.0 or both.

